{
  "case_id": "2021-20-303",
  "document_hash": "2975fcfa2803e7c45e5e9840c74d2c88c99594d6bbfa4a9ad116f55b0cd69bc2",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-303",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2975fcfa2803e7c45e5e9840c74d2c88c99594d6bbfa4a9ad116f55b0cd69bc2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2975fcfa2803-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The court of appeals erred in holding that Congress's decision not to extend its Supplemental Security Income program to Puerto Rico lacks a rational basis."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-303",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2975fcfa2803e7c45e5e9840c74d2c88c99594d6bbfa4a9ad116f55b0cd69bc2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2975fcfa2803-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress could reasonably take those considerations into account when deciding that Puerto Rico's residents would receive some federal benefits but not others."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-303",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2975fcfa2803e7c45e5e9840c74d2c88c99594d6bbfa4a9ad116f55b0cd69bc2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2975fcfa2803-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Gannon, do you think that the Territory Clause is enough of a -- a source of authority for the government or Congress to have a rational basis to do what it's doing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-20-303",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2975fcfa2803e7c45e5e9840c74d2c88c99594d6bbfa4a9ad116f55b0cd69bc2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2975fcfa2803-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do the Insular Cases have anything to do with this litigation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-303",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2975fcfa2803e7c45e5e9840c74d2c88c99594d6bbfa4a9ad116f55b0cd69bc2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2975fcfa2803-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, if that's true, why -- why -- why shouldn't we just admit the Insular Cases were incorrectly decided?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. GANNON",
      "case_id": "2021-20-303",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2975fcfa2803e7c45e5e9840c74d2c88c99594d6bbfa4a9ad116f55b0cd69bc2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2975fcfa2803-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We think that here, it -- it -- the rational basis standard that the Court articulated in Torres and applied in Rosario would allow Congress to take into account this consideration that -- that there is less tax revenue coming in."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2021-20-303",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2975fcfa2803e7c45e5e9840c74d2c88c99594d6bbfa4a9ad116f55b0cd69bc2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2975fcfa2803-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How does the fact that Puerto Rico residents are a politically powerless minority -- you're just telling us that, can't protect itself the way Mississippi can -- and has been subject to, by your own admission right now, a history of discrimination -- the Insular Cases are a prime example of that; just look at their language -- how does this factor into your argument on rational basis?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. GANNON",
      "case_id": "2021-20-303",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2975fcfa2803e7c45e5e9840c74d2c88c99594d6bbfa4a9ad116f55b0cd69bc2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2975fcfa2803-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They are U.S. citizens, but there is no evidence here linking this exclusion to ethnicity or --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. FERRE",
      "case_id": "2021-20-303",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2975fcfa2803e7c45e5e9840c74d2c88c99594d6bbfa4a9ad116f55b0cd69bc2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2975fcfa2803-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But it is also simply irrational to treat Mr. Vaello-Madero differently just because he's now in Puerto Rico. That is what the lower courts unanimously held."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-303",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2975fcfa2803e7c45e5e9840c74d2c88c99594d6bbfa4a9ad116f55b0cd69bc2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2975fcfa2803-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Okay. So let's assume that someone who is of Italian descent has lived in New York City all of his life and decides: You know, Puerto Rico's really a nice place. I think I'm going to move to Puerto Rico. And assume after that that the exact same thing happens to him as happened to Respondent here, but he's Italian. How would you analyze that? Would it be any different?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-303",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2975fcfa2803e7c45e5e9840c74d2c88c99594d6bbfa4a9ad116f55b0cd69bc2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2975fcfa2803-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Do you have any cases in which that has been the case, where you have equal protection cases involving women or Blacks or members of Hispanic groups, et cetera, Native Heritage Reporting Corporation"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-20-303",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2975fcfa2803e7c45e5e9840c74d2c88c99594d6bbfa4a9ad116f55b0cd69bc2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2975fcfa2803-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So do -- do I understand that -- that argument to be that the Territory Clause has a -- a sort of implicit expiration date attached to it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ferre",
      "case_id": "2021-20-303",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2975fcfa2803e7c45e5e9840c74d2c88c99594d6bbfa4a9ad116f55b0cd69bc2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2975fcfa2803-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that the Court should take and the Court has in the past certain -- certainly taken into account the fact of a -- an individual or a group's political powerlessness."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-20-303",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2975fcfa2803e7c45e5e9840c74d2c88c99594d6bbfa4a9ad116f55b0cd69bc2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2975fcfa2803-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Might you still apply for the waiver if you don't prevail in this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Curtis E. Gannon",
      "case_id": "2021-20-303",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2975fcfa2803e7c45e5e9840c74d2c88c99594d6bbfa4a9ad116f55b0cd69bc2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2975fcfa2803-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, the territories clause -- the Territory Clause does not have an except -- an -- an expiration date, and, if it did, the Court's analysis in cases like Aurelius would have been completely different."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2021-20-303",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "2975fcfa2803e7c45e5e9840c74d2c88c99594d6bbfa4a9ad116f55b0cd69bc2",
